static class JournalText {
internal static readonly string[] SceneNames={"THE LAST CAMPSITE","A ROAD THAT LED NOWHERE","THE WAITING LIST","NO MORE ROOM","KEEP THE LIGHT ON","THE EVACUATION LINE"};
 internal static readonly string[] SceneNotes={
 "Mara,\n\nWe stayed another night. The kettle is still warm and your scarf is hanging by the tent. If you find this, follow the road toward the forest. We left the little lantern for you.\n\nI told him you would come back.\n\n- E.",
 "The highway sign said evacuation was twelve kilometres away. We drove until the fuel ran out. Then we walked.\n\nDad put the keys in my pocket and said we would need them when we came home.\n\nI still have them.",
 "TRIAGE REGISTER / DAY 11\n\nBeds: 14. Patients: 63.\n\nThe people outside keep knocking. We stopped answering when the generator failed. Someone is still moving in the ward.\n\nPlease do not tell their families we had room.",
 "We buried six today. No names on the last two. There was a photograph in one coat, but the rain had taken the faces.\n\nIf anyone comes looking, tell them we tried to make this place quiet.",
 "If the light goes out, do not leave the room.\n\nIf someone calls your name from the corridor, do not answer.\n\nI know that sounds cruel. I heard my brother yesterday. He has been gone for three weeks.",
 "CHECKPOINT LOG / FINAL ENTRY\n\nThe buses never came.\n\nWe kept the barrier closed because those were the orders. By dawn there were shoes and bags everywhere. No one left to argue with us.\n\nI am leaving the gate open."};

